// The GTK 4 platform: every node a GTK widget, placed in SNGL over a C
// runtime every language calls (rt/), and its widgets, one component per GTK
// class of the bundled GIR named as C names it (`GtkButton`), in
// widgets.sngl, which gtk4gen writes. A program names one as `gtk4.GtkButton`,
// as it names `html.button`.
//
// gtk4.sngl overrides each stdlib component with those widgets and the
// runtime's own (a toplevel, a canvas, a flow of rich text). A program may
// still import `gir:Gtk-4.0`, which the library's gir: scheme declares from the
// introspection data the `gir` option selects, through the platform's Look and
// `setLook`; a class there calls its C functions directly.
